WEBVTT

00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:07.900
You touched my hand when I stretched them out so far...

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:18.950
Final Episode

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:18.950
Star Sky Loop

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:21.700
Just one word is fine.

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.540
Just voice your dreams.

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:28.670
It's your first step and first sign to realization.

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:32.800
Ask yourself what is it that you like?

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:34.930
Your answers will...

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:39.890
blow your questions high into the sky.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:36.340
Even more...

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:38.220
Like fireworks...

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:46.440
Even though we should all try to be more honest we ourselves, we can't.

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:53.440
Maybe I should try summoning my soul as a child?

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:59.950
What touched my hand when i stretched them out so far...

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:05.120
was a Supernova that suddenly appear to this new night.

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:11.090
For millions of light years, it never stops inside of me.

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:19.300
The longer I gaze, the more power my eyes absorb...

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:24.560
and that's because... because I'm a star too!

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:31.020
We enter the final day of our inter-school winter camp

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:31.020
On the other hand, Roma and Oumi prepare for their exams

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:36.030
The two had met back in their childhood...

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:36.030
But that will be saved for the Special

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:06.430
What a fabulous morning!

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:09.480
A fabulous <i>afternoon</i>, you mean.

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:10.810
Nonetheless, good morning.

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:15.570
Behold!

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:17.990
The bath in the snow!

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:21.990
It’s so cold!

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:23.490
Someone hit me with some water!

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:24.620
Here you go!

00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:26.040
Sayo-chin! Sayo-chin!

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:27.160
Let’s make a snowman!

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:29.040
Get in the <i>bath</i> first!

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:30.750
Hot! Hot!

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:31.960
I can’t! I can’t!

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:33.420
Guys, calm down!

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:37.840
Oh, I’m in heaven.

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:41.010
Nothing like this to follow a night of stargazing.

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:45.220
It’s so great to have such a nice bath nearby.

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:47.310
You got that right.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:51.150
The inn has a good bath, but this one is so much more liberating.

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:53.770
Unless I dunk myself in here after the night,

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:55.230
I can’t keep living.

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:58.900
Last night just ended up being a gaming night.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:02.240
The sky didn’t clear up until right before sunrise.

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:04.530
We’re heading home tomorrow,

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:06.540
so tonight will be our final chance.

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:10.580
And we didn’t get to stargaze on the first night for some reason...

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:13.130
I-I’m sorry!

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:14.750
Kidding.

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:18.630
We’ve done it before, so we can’t really blame you.

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:21.260
It was back in the summer camp, during our freshman year.

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:24.970
Minami went off on her own, just to buy a drink.

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:29.520
I chased after her, and we both ended up lost in the mist.

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:32.020
It was just us, all alone on a mountain in summer.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:34.270
Yeah.

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:35.310
This is seriously scary!

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:35.900
But just like the other day,

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:37.230
Fire!

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:39.740
our seniors fired the surge cannons.

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:45.120
When I saw Edogawa-kun using the flash on his camera, it all came back to me.

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:47.830
The sky almost never cleared up that year,

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:50.460
so we ended up firing tons of those into the clouds.

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:52.000
Discussing our fetishes.

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:53.210
Looking back,

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:56.920
that was when our road opened up to us.

00:03:57.800 --> 00:03:58.550
Ann!

00:03:58.880 --> 00:03:59.760
Surge cannon!

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:02.590
Make sure you pass that tradition down to future astronomy clubs!

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:04.970
It’s... a tradition...?

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:08.890
But, Fluffy-chan, you really must be more careful.

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:11.020
Stores are farther away in these mountains.

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:11.980
Yes, ma’am!

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:12.730
Good?

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:13.310
Yes!

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:14.810
On another note...

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:17.270
Yaraicchi, they look so much bigger without any clothing!

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:18.480
Amazing!

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:21.530
And you have such smooth skin!

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:22.280
Can I touch it?

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:24.240
Screw it, I’ll do it anyways!

00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:26.660
Oh, don’t feel embarrassed.

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:28.200
What about you, Hoshimi-chan?

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:30.040
Just what I was expecting!

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:31.580
You’re up next, Fluffy-chan!

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:34.540
Stop calling me Fluffy!

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:33.790
Say...

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:34.670
Hmm?

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:36.250
You know!

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:38.170
I think they’re doing this to me on purpose!

00:04:38.170 --> 00:04:39.960
They’re luring me to their bath!

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:41.380
Very well, then!

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:42.590
I’ll take a peep!

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:43.880
If that’s what you wish,

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:45.720
I’ll take a peep, O’ dear cuckoo!

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:46.930
Restrain yourself!

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:48.470
O’ dear cuckoo!

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:49.260
Don’t make me touch you!

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:51.020
Stop!

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:52.730
Three... Two... One...

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:53.940
Saku-chan!

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:54.770
Sou-nii!

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:56.480
How’s the bath on your side?

00:04:57.440 --> 00:04:58.650
Want me to wash your back?

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:00.940
Did you bring towels to wash yourselves with?

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:00.900
Hey!

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:03.740
Hey, Mihoshi!

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:05.240
A girl shouldn’t be peeping!

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:07.620
Then I shall, as well!

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:08.740
Stop, Edogawa!

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:10.030
Don’t stop me, Ooyagi!

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:11.870
Hey, are you listening to me, Saku-chan?

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:14.160
Make sure to keep yourselves warm.

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:15.330
Hoshimi-chan never ceases to amaze me.

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:23.010
Man... it was horrible...

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:24.510
Really horrible...

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:25.840
Like, <i>extremely</i> horrible...

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:36.940
Here, you must be exhausted.

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:40.360
After you fry your brain studying, you should eat some sugar.

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:41.570
Oumi-san.

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:47.110
Say, Roma-kun.

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:51.410
Can we... hang out a bit tomorrow?

00:05:54.700 --> 00:05:55.330
Found it!

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:56.120
It’s this one.

00:06:00.170 --> 00:06:00.500
Well?

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:03.210
Don’t you think it’s perfect for what we’re doing?

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:04.800
Yes, it is.

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:11.390
Well, thank you for today.

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:21.730
Can we... hang out for a while longer?

00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:29.360
Just because we’re preparing for exams doesn’t mean we can’t eat out.

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:32.070
I’ve actually already made a reservation.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:40.920
Welcome.

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:43.540
I presume you are Miss Oumi.

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:44.960
This way, please.

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:47.840
No need to be so tense.

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:50.050
I come here often with my family.

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:52.680
May I take your order?

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:54.350
Let’s see...

00:06:55.180 --> 00:06:57.220
May I have herbal soup and spice gruel?

00:06:58.100 --> 00:06:58.850
And can I...

00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:05.570
It’s been a while since I last had an actual meal.

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:06.860
That’s good to hear.

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:09.860
I was hoping you’d finish it slowly.

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:11.910
I think it’s almost time.

00:07:12.110 --> 00:07:12.740
Oh...

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:14.910
Is this place closing?

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:16.990
I guess I took a little too long.

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:18.750
That’s not it.

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:20.330
It’s almost time for our main dish.

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:28.970
Not yet.

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:30.510
Not yet.

00:07:32.050 --> 00:07:33.590
No peeking.

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:38.350
All right.

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:39.430
Open them up.

00:07:52.150 --> 00:07:53.860
It’s the terrace of this restaurant.

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:57.080
They keep the terrace closed during the winter, so I asked them to open it, just for us.

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:01.870
Here.

00:08:02.420 --> 00:08:03.170
Look over there.

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:07.040
The city lights are a little distracting, but I think these binoculars will help.

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:16.100
Extending Canis Major’s legs, following it to the red star near the horizon.

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:22.230
Canopus!

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:25.600
I’m so glad that you can see it!

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:28.770
I would’ve looked like an idiot if you couldn’t.

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:32.400
It’s my first time... seeing the actual star.

00:08:32.650 --> 00:08:34.030
That’s even better!

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:38.700
I... was worried.

00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:40.790
You looked like you were pushing yourself.

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:47.250
Though... I guess there aren’t many exam takers who don’t need to push themselves.

00:08:47.710 --> 00:08:53.300
But... I thought maybe you were over pressured and weren’t eating properly.

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:55.630
Roma-kun...

00:08:57.470 --> 00:09:00.510
You’ll be fine as long as you relax and watch your health.

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:03.480
Oumi-san.

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:08.190
Now then, let’s go home before we catch a cold.

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:09.860
It’s getting kinda late, too.

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:10.570
Oh—

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:14.400
Thank you, Oumi-san.

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:18.910
But... why did you do all of this for me?

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:23.250
You’re... going to make me say it?

00:09:38.090 --> 00:09:39.600
Oh, whatever.

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:41.310
Let’s go back in.

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:45.430
But before that...

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:54.320
Let’s take it easy when spring comes around.

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:55.150
Of course.

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:38.650
Moon setting... and gone.

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:40.450
Let’s get going.

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:43.830
Photograph Group, gather around the shoot location.

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:46.700
You can move around a bit, but don’t go out too far.

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:50.250
We’ll keep recording the video from the observatory.

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:51.540
I pray for you all...

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:53.340
that this last night of the camp will be the best.

00:10:53.380 --> 00:10:54.630
Yeah!

00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:57.510
All right, let’s do this, guys!

00:10:57.550 --> 00:10:58.720
Yeah!

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:02.760
With the Photography Club’s cooperation, I got as many as I could borrow.

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:06.270
I’m going to show off my good side, and appeal to everyone!

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:10.560
Guys! I’m making a nice, warm drink for you all.

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:12.020
Thank you!

00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:25.280
I never knew that winter was this cold, and that there were so many stars.

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:29.460
In the city, you can only see the brighter stars,

00:11:29.870 --> 00:11:31.710
which made the constellations easier to spot,

00:11:32.630 --> 00:11:36.090
so I had the wrong idea about exactly how many stars there were.

00:11:37.420 --> 00:11:40.720
The Winter Triangle consists of the magnitude 1 star of Orion, the orange Betelgeuse,

00:11:41.180 --> 00:11:46.760
Procyon of Canis Minor, and Sirius of Canis Major.

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:50.810
Then when you add Rigel of Orion, Aldebaran of Taurus,

00:11:51.230 --> 00:11:56.520
Capella of Auriga, and Pollux of Gemini, you get the Winter Hexagon.

00:11:57.690 --> 00:12:00.690
I thought I had seen it a million times already, but this is an entirely new experience.

00:12:02.070 --> 00:12:03.660
What did we tell you, eh, Ooyagi-kun?

00:12:05.070 --> 00:12:07.120
The winter has seven magnitude 1 stars,

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:08.620
so it’s even more worth the watch.

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:10.290
Please don’t scare me like that!

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:14.670
The stars are definitely brighter,

00:12:15.210 --> 00:12:17.090
but the atmosphere here is also different.

00:12:17.380 --> 00:12:19.210
The sky seems much darker...

00:12:19.210 --> 00:12:20.170
Or am I just high?

00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:22.130
No, you’re not.

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:24.340
The sun sets quite early during winter.

00:12:24.970 --> 00:12:27.680
It’s due to that that there’s less afterglow.

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:31.310
Also, it’s much clearer because the air is dry.

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:37.110
That’s also why you can sometimes see an astonishing amount of stars from the city.

00:12:38.270 --> 00:12:42.110
Brighter stars, a darker curtain, and a clearer sky.

00:12:42.780 --> 00:12:45.950
This refreshing glow is brought about by all those factors.

00:12:46.740 --> 00:12:51.910
Yeah, but it isn’t the best idea to look through a telescope on a day like this.

00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:55.080
When the stars are twinkling so clearly?

00:12:55.420 --> 00:12:56.540
That’s exactly why.

00:12:57.130 --> 00:13:01.260
When they are twinkling more, it means that the air in the sky is unstable.

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:02.760
Scintillation.

00:13:03.170 --> 00:13:07.180
Regardless of how clear the sky is, the stars we see get distorted by the turbulent atmosphere.

00:13:07.640 --> 00:13:10.680
It’s similar to how you can’t see well inside the water when it’s wavy.

00:13:11.140 --> 00:13:12.930
When it’s calm, the water’s clear, right?

00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:16.230
We’re currently filming from the observatory because of the scintillation.

00:13:17.150 --> 00:13:19.150
We can enjoy the fluctuation as a type of movement,

00:13:19.270 --> 00:13:22.030
and we can take snapshots of scenes with good footage.

00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:23.530
That’s pretty cool.

00:13:23.740 --> 00:13:25.280
Though we still look through telescopes.

00:13:26.410 --> 00:13:31.290
Also, there are lots of open clusters in winter that can be seen with binoculars and smaller telescopes,

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:33.410
so it’ll keep you up all night.

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:35.620
Come take a look, Saku-chan! It’s the Pleiades!

00:13:35.910 --> 00:13:36.620
The Pleiades?!

00:13:37.710 --> 00:13:40.840
The pretty sisters that run away from Orion are so moe!

00:13:40.960 --> 00:13:42.250
All right! Next one!

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:43.340
Let’s see M 35!

00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:45.090
M 35!

00:13:45.420 --> 00:13:47.630
Is it moe that gives you strength?!

00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:48.840
Is it?!

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:52.810
A-Anyway, it’s also time I get started on taking pictures.

00:13:53.350 --> 00:13:55.140
Uhh, this goes here...

00:13:55.600 --> 00:13:58.190
Edogawa always did this for me.

00:13:58.770 --> 00:13:59.810
No problem.

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:00.860
We’re in no rush.

00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:06.740
But it would be better to lower this tripod.

00:14:07.150 --> 00:14:08.740
Put release button here...

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:11.660
Do you have a pocket heater?

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:12.790
These?

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:15.410
Not the disposable ones...

00:14:15.910 --> 00:14:18.620
If you attach a pocket heater that uses tree ashes like this,

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:20.880
you can prevent the lens from fogging up.

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:23.590
Wow, you’re amazing.

00:14:23.920 --> 00:14:26.300
You can find everything in an outdoor-goods store.

00:14:27.260 --> 00:14:29.010
No fair!

00:14:29.470 --> 00:14:30.430
Guys!

00:14:31.050 --> 00:14:32.600
How about a little break?

00:14:33.010 --> 00:14:35.060
Oh, this warms me up.

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:36.140
Here’s one for you.

00:14:36.180 --> 00:14:37.100
It’s good.

00:14:37.560 --> 00:14:38.640
So good!

00:14:39.310 --> 00:14:42.360
This’ll be the last year I get to drink your amazake.

00:14:42.440 --> 00:14:43.440
Kawamura-san...

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:48.030
It was the best, Sakai-chan.

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:49.450
Minami-san...

00:14:50.070 --> 00:14:51.070
Group hug!

00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:53.700
So, are you ever going to find yourself a husband?

00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:55.990
No, please don’t say that.

00:14:56.870 --> 00:14:59.870
I can’t believe those two will be gone soon...

00:15:01.130 --> 00:15:04.800
I wonder if I’m really up to being a leader.

00:15:05.460 --> 00:15:06.510
You’ll do just fine.

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:08.340
Oh, no.

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:09.590
Did I say that out loud?

00:15:10.010 --> 00:15:10.970
I’m sorry.

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:12.340
I overheard it by accident.

00:15:13.010 --> 00:15:15.810
But I know you guys will be just fine.

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:18.020
Seeing your school’s club...

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:22.810
really shows me that everyone has fun differently.

00:15:23.520 --> 00:15:26.360
So... I think you’ll be fine leading in your own way.

00:15:26.940 --> 00:15:28.780
In fact, I should be worrying about <i>us</i>.

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:31.450
We have no telescope, and we’ll just be a fan club if we don’t find new members.

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:33.490
I wonder if we’ll still be a club next year.

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:34.700
That’s terrible.

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:35.950
That’s right.

00:15:36.080 --> 00:15:38.160
I don’t know what you’re feeling insecure about,

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:40.660
but I know you’re always doing your best.

00:15:41.250 --> 00:15:42.250
You too, Aizawa.

00:15:43.460 --> 00:15:44.880
Senpai.

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:47.840
Hey! Let’s get off this subject!

00:15:48.630 --> 00:15:51.300
Hoshimi-chan, is there anything you want to see?

00:15:51.470 --> 00:15:54.550
Oh, you haven’t seen Saturn yet, right?

00:15:54.930 --> 00:15:57.510
It’s still a bit hard to spot, but do you want to see it?

00:15:57.720 --> 00:15:58.470
Saturn?!

00:15:59.270 --> 00:16:02.850
Oh, but she was saying she wanted to see it with her equipment.

00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:04.940
That’s what I had in mind.

00:16:07.570 --> 00:16:08.480
Tada!

00:16:10.940 --> 00:16:12.910
Wow, are these eyepieces?!

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:14.450
Where did you get these?

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:16.780
And these are really high-quality!

00:16:22.120 --> 00:16:24.420
Did we have eyepieces?

00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:25.420
I dunno...

00:16:25.920 --> 00:16:28.920
But what’s with these random stickers?

00:16:32.090 --> 00:16:34.840
Mihoshi... aren’t those...

00:16:35.260 --> 00:16:36.140
You haven’t forgotten yet?

00:16:36.600 --> 00:16:38.010
We scribbled all over that together.

00:16:38.390 --> 00:16:39.350
So they are.

00:16:40.770 --> 00:16:43.390
The actual telescope broke during the accident,

00:16:43.690 --> 00:16:46.270
so I could only bring the eyepieces,

00:16:46.900 --> 00:16:49.980
but I really wanted to bring something we could all use.

00:16:51.490 --> 00:16:56.280
I’m happy we can see Saturn together, because my daddy really liked it, too.

00:16:57.370 --> 00:16:58.080
Look!

00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:02.540
The one next to Leo is Saturn.

00:17:03.790 --> 00:17:07.380
Ursa Major, Arcturus, and Spica.

00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:11.670
We can already see the spring sky we all saw together.

00:17:16.760 --> 00:17:18.680
The sky has rotated a full circle.

00:17:20.850 --> 00:17:22.100
One star after another...

00:17:22.310 --> 00:17:24.140
A relay of seasons that connect them all together.

00:17:24.850 --> 00:17:27.600
A new relay’s about to start.

00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:33.110
Hey!

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:34.950
Since it’s your eyepiece,

00:17:35.110 --> 00:17:36.740
why don’t you find Saturn?

00:17:37.070 --> 00:17:38.740
Come, come, Sakkun!

00:17:39.410 --> 00:17:39.910
Me?!

00:17:41.030 --> 00:17:42.200
Stop that!

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:45.290
Move this and this.

00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:46.500
Hold on.

00:17:47.290 --> 00:17:48.920
Take your time.

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:49.670
This way?

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:51.500
No, this way.

00:17:51.630 --> 00:17:52.250
Too far.

00:17:52.630 --> 00:17:54.630
Umm...

00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:56.970
I’m sweating.

00:17:57.180 --> 00:17:58.840
Stop looking at me, please.

00:17:59.680 --> 00:18:00.970
Don’t worry.

00:18:01.050 --> 00:18:01.810
Calm down.

00:18:11.980 --> 00:18:13.980
After you find it, focus the lens.

00:18:22.330 --> 00:18:25.290
This... is Saturn?

00:18:26.120 --> 00:18:26.410
So?

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:27.710
Can you see the rings?

00:18:29.250 --> 00:18:30.750
I think it’s thanks to the eyepiece.

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:32.250
It’s really clear.

00:18:31.380 --> 00:18:35.760
I look up at the sky, and I think of you…

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:33.590
Though it is fluctuating a bit.

00:18:34.300 --> 00:18:35.510
Can I see too?

00:18:36.050 --> 00:18:39.430
but I can’t find the words,

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:42.720
I want to tell you,

00:18:41.220 --> 00:18:44.600
<i>It was... a small image, swaying in the sky.</i>

00:18:42.720 --> 00:18:45.220
but they just slip away…

00:18:45.560 --> 00:18:48.890
almost like Shooting Stars.

00:18:46.220 --> 00:18:47.560
It’s so small!

00:18:47.850 --> 00:18:49.560
But it’s so cool!

00:18:49.390 --> 00:18:53.480
In this Wave of Silence,

00:18:50.940 --> 00:18:52.310
I can really make out the rings.

00:18:52.730 --> 00:18:54.230
It’s like Galileo’s drawings.

00:18:53.860 --> 00:18:57.860
a ray of light flickers the darkness

00:18:55.610 --> 00:18:58.070
What... is this feeling?

00:18:58.320 --> 00:19:03.160
playing with my memories

00:19:00.240 --> 00:19:03.160
I can understand why they all want to see it.

00:19:03.160 --> 00:19:09.000
and releasing my heart.

00:19:05.490 --> 00:19:05.990
Yeah.

00:19:09.830 --> 00:19:11.960
Into the future,

00:19:09.960 --> 00:19:10.790
In the solar system...

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:13.880
it’s the sixth closest planet from the Sun.

00:19:11.960 --> 00:19:20.510
I will have these feelings again!

00:19:15.250 --> 00:19:18.880
Who knows how many people have seen it with their eyes.

00:19:20.630 --> 00:19:24.930
So many people have passed down their excitement to bring this to the present.

00:19:20.930 --> 00:19:24.930
No worries, I’m not alone.

00:19:25.180 --> 00:19:30.020
You have taught me I’m not alone.

00:19:26.310 --> 00:19:29.100
I’m... going to do the same.

00:19:30.020 --> 00:19:38.940
Listen to my “Twinkle” story!

00:19:30.060 --> 00:19:31.520
That’s our girl.

00:19:31.770 --> 00:19:33.060
Well said.

00:19:34.060 --> 00:19:36.900
Come springtime at our new schools...

00:19:37.940 --> 00:19:39.570
we’ll spread this excitement around.

00:19:39.070 --> 00:19:43.120
Maybe my voice would reach you.

00:19:39.900 --> 00:19:40.950
Me too.

00:19:41.110 --> 00:19:44.490
I may not be very reliable, but I’ll do my best.

00:19:44.490 --> 00:19:49.370
I look up at the sky, surrounded by Stardust!

00:19:45.030 --> 00:19:45.660
Ann...

00:19:46.410 --> 00:19:47.240
Hug!

00:19:47.490 --> 00:19:48.370
Thanks!

00:19:48.450 --> 00:19:49.710
It’s been a blast with you.

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:52.170
And thank you, Souei High School.

00:19:52.710 --> 00:19:53.830
Same here.

00:19:57.590 --> 00:20:01.970
I wonder if we shed tears

00:20:00.380 --> 00:20:02.720
To the next stars that shall come around...

00:20:02.970 --> 00:20:04.550
A blessing!

00:20:06.600 --> 00:20:08.010
All right!

00:20:52.350 --> 00:20:54.560
Oh, I’m in heaven.

00:20:54.730 --> 00:20:57.270
Camps are all about the bath.

00:20:57.360 --> 00:20:58.360
Is that you two I hear?

00:20:58.980 --> 00:21:00.820
Hey, have you written <i>anything</i>?

00:21:01.110 --> 00:21:03.990
Don’t worry, we have.

00:21:04.400 --> 00:21:06.570
You’ll be juniors next year.

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:08.950
Act more appropriately as Literature Club members.

00:21:09.030 --> 00:21:09.910
Yes, ma’am!

00:21:10.040 --> 00:21:12.160
But Senpai, you’re talking to a bamboo pipe.

00:21:13.040 --> 00:21:14.500
Hey, a shooting star!

00:21:33.270 --> 00:21:36.020
<i>Under the same stars and the same sky...</i>

00:21:37.560 --> 00:21:40.570
<i>may many relays be shared.</i>

00:21:50.620 --> 00:21:53.410
Everyone watch out!

00:21:57.620 --> 00:21:59.130
Oww...

00:22:00.670 --> 00:22:01.880
What are you doing?!

00:22:02.130 --> 00:22:03.000
Mihoshi!

00:22:05.010 --> 00:22:07.800
Well, new students are coming in.

00:22:07.930 --> 00:22:09.510
We need to stand out.

00:22:09.590 --> 00:22:10.930
But why that costume?

00:22:11.220 --> 00:22:12.010
Aren’t I cute?

00:22:12.390 --> 00:22:13.010
No.

00:22:13.850 --> 00:22:15.020
<i>Spring has arrived.</i>

00:22:16.180 --> 00:22:18.270
<i>President Roma passed his exam...</i>

00:22:18.440 --> 00:22:20.650
<i>and will be living a campus life with Oumi-san.</i>

00:22:21.310 --> 00:22:25.530
<i>We all moved up a grade, and new students came to our school.</i>

00:22:27.570 --> 00:22:28.700
And the Astronomy Club...

00:22:29.200 --> 00:22:30.910
is in a frenzy to stay alive.

00:22:31.830 --> 00:22:35.500
We’re going to get at least one new member!

00:22:36.000 --> 00:22:39.460
Succeeding President Roma, and taking on his responsibility,

00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:44.250
I, Akeno Mihoshi, shall attack anything with all my might!

00:22:45.420 --> 00:22:46.760
Is this going to work...?

00:22:47.090 --> 00:22:49.130
I think you’d be more fitting for the role, Sayo-senpai.

00:22:49.380 --> 00:22:52.100
But Mihoshi is the most enthusiastic of us here.

00:22:52.390 --> 00:22:55.180
Well... finding one new person shouldn’t be that hard.

00:22:55.970 --> 00:22:56.980
Hey, Edogawa!

00:22:57.020 --> 00:22:58.140
Get serious!

00:22:59.270 --> 00:23:01.230
I’m not in the same class anymore...

00:23:01.480 --> 00:23:03.150
I can’t lose this club too...

00:23:03.940 --> 00:23:04.980
That’s right.

00:23:05.070 --> 00:23:06.440
We’re not in the same class anymore.

00:23:07.070 --> 00:23:09.570
It’s a shame, since we were the Astronomy Club Trio.

00:23:11.200 --> 00:23:14.200
C-Can I poke my head into your classroom?

00:23:14.280 --> 00:23:14.830
Of cour—

00:23:14.660 --> 00:23:15.660
Thank you!!

00:23:15.660 --> 00:23:17.500
That alone gives me strength!

00:23:17.660 --> 00:23:18.160
Huh?

00:23:18.660 --> 00:23:19.920
What’s that, Saku-chan?

00:23:20.330 --> 00:23:22.040
Well...

00:23:22.630 --> 00:23:25.880
We published a few wall newspapers last year,

00:23:26.250 --> 00:23:28.380
but I thought we should try harder this year.

00:23:28.800 --> 00:23:31.130
So I made a flayers for the club as our first publication...

00:23:32.010 --> 00:23:32.680
It’s good.

00:23:32.300 --> 00:23:39.770
You touched my hand when I stretched them out so far...

00:23:32.720 --> 00:23:33.640
It’s great!

00:23:34.300 --> 00:23:35.180
This is great!

00:23:35.560 --> 00:23:36.810
You go, Saku-chan!

00:23:37.390 --> 00:23:38.520
All right!

00:23:38.640 --> 00:23:39.680
Let’s do this!

00:23:42.850 --> 00:23:44.360
Come stop by!

00:23:44.520 --> 00:23:45.730
We’re the Astronomy Club!

00:23:46.070 --> 00:23:47.070
We’re the Astronomy Club.

00:23:47.900 --> 00:23:48.610
Here’s a flyer.

00:23:49.950 --> 00:23:51.070
I’m from the Astronomy Club.

00:23:51.280 --> 00:23:53.570
Just one word is fine.

00:23:51.360 --> 00:23:52.200
Here’s a flyer.

00:23:53.570 --> 00:23:54.490
I’m from the Astronomy Club.

00:23:53.950 --> 00:23:56.410
Just voice your dreams.

00:23:56.200 --> 00:23:58.950
My, are you still planning to continue?

00:23:56.700 --> 00:24:00.540
It's your first step and first sign to realization.

00:23:59.540 --> 00:24:00.870
Kotozuka-senpai.

00:24:01.330 --> 00:24:04.750
Congratulations on winning the Presidential election again.

00:24:02.120 --> 00:24:04.670
Ask yourself what is it that you like?

00:24:04.750 --> 00:24:06.630
Th-Thank you...

00:24:04.920 --> 00:24:06.800
Your answers will...

00:24:06.800 --> 00:24:11.760
blow your questions high into the sky.

00:24:07.500 --> 00:24:08.210
Even more...

00:24:08.050 --> 00:24:09.130
What a waste.

00:24:08.960 --> 00:24:10.090
Like fireworks...

00:24:09.590 --> 00:24:11.590
You can write so well...

00:24:11.760 --> 00:24:18.310
Even though we should all try to be more honest we ourselves, we can't.

00:24:12.050 --> 00:24:13.300
Oh my God!

00:24:13.550 --> 00:24:15.890
Kotozuka-senpai’s complimenting a paper!

00:24:15.970 --> 00:24:17.010
You girls!

00:24:18.520 --> 00:24:20.600
Hey, don’t you have something to do?

00:24:18.560 --> 00:24:25.310
Maybe I should try summoning my soul as a child?

00:24:20.770 --> 00:24:22.230
What are these?

00:24:25.810 --> 00:24:31.820
What touched my hand when i stretched them out so far...

00:24:29.690 --> 00:24:31.070
Everyone!

00:24:31.400 --> 00:24:33.360
Hello!

00:24:31.950 --> 00:24:36.990
was a Supernova that suddenly appear to this new night.

00:24:32.740 --> 00:24:33.320
Mii-chan!

00:24:33.700 --> 00:24:34.410
Hey!

00:24:34.610 --> 00:24:36.830
Who said you could use the roof?!

00:24:37.080 --> 00:24:42.960
For millions of light years, it never stops inside of me.

00:24:37.490 --> 00:24:40.500
Do you like stars?

00:24:39.370 --> 00:24:40.750
Yeah!

00:24:41.540 --> 00:24:42.870
The Astronomy Club...

00:24:42.960 --> 00:24:51.170
The longer I gaze, the more power my eyes absorb...

00:24:43.290 --> 00:24:48.670
is really, really, really, really looking for new members right now!

00:24:49.090 --> 00:24:49.840
Let’s watch...

00:24:50.300 --> 00:24:50.920
the stars...

00:24:51.170 --> 00:24:56.430
and that's because... because I'm a star too!

00:24:52.340 --> 00:24:54.930
together!
